# Copy to `.env` and adjust. `.env` is git-ignored (it's your live config).

# --- The LLM door: one pipe from the sandbox to ONE host port ------------------
# Your OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM, llama-server…), reached
# from the sandbox at http://llm:8080/v1. Under `airlock` this comes from the
# PROJECT's config instead (LOCAL_MODEL=endpoint + LLM_HOST/LLM_PORT/LLM_MODEL, the
# key in the project's secrets file) and the picker sets LLM_TARGET_PORT itself;
# set these here only for raw `bin/harness` callers, whose door
# forwards to LLM_HOST:LLM_TARGET_PORT (default host.docker.internal:8000).
LLM_HOST=host.docker.internal
# LLM_TARGET_PORT=11434
# LLM_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
#
# LOCAL_MODEL=off (airlock) starts no door at all. Servers this machine should start
# and stop itself are registered by a backends plugin (a host-side shell file:
# backends.sh at the kit root, or set AIRLOCK_BACKENDS to its path; example in
# templates/backends.example.sh) — see README.md, "LLM backends".

# Claude Code model. Empty = Claude Code picks its own default.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# Pin harness versions for reproducible image builds (default: latest).
# CLAUDE_CODE_VERSION=
# CODEX_VERSION=
# OPENCODE_VERSION=
# COPILOT_VERSION=

# Component version pins. Which components a stack installs is airlock.json's
# business (repo root); these only say WHICH version of each.
JDK_VERSION=25
ANGULAR_VERSION=21
# DOTNET_VERSION=10.0.203

# Playwright + headless Chromium, for projects that opt in with COMPONENTS=playwright
# (drive the app under test / local e2e; needs no runtime egress). Pin for
# reproducible browser builds, and match a project's own playwright dep to avoid a
# runtime re-download.
# PLAYWRIGHT_VERSION=

# Image recipe. Default = dev/Dockerfile, the one parametrised sandbox image
# (airlock.json + the project's STACK= decide what goes into it). Set these only to
# build a recipe of your own, e.g. one with a pre-warmed offline dependency cache;
# the recipe is looked up inside DEV_CONTEXT (default ./dev).
# DEV_CONTEXT=./dev
# DEV_DOCKERFILE=Dockerfile.custom

# Point Codex (or any OpenAI SDK) at the real OpenAI API instead of the
# local LLM door. Real OpenAI also needs .openai.com on the whitelist — under
# airlock that comes from HARNESS=codex (proxy/whitelist.d/harness-codex.txt).
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Mount host credentials instead of the per-project control-dir state/ dirs
# (or the ./state/ fallback used by raw bin/harness callers). Prefer setting
# these in the project's own config (`airlock config --edit`), not here. gh and codex keep theirs in plain
# files, so this works; ~/.claude does NOT carry auth on macOS (Keychain — see
# README.md, "Credentials").
# GH_STATE=~/.config/gh
# CODEX_STATE=~/.codex

# Credentials: under `airlock` these belong in the PROJECT's secrets file
# (`airlock config --secrets` → ~/.airlock/<project>-<hash6>/env, mode 0600), not
# here — airlock exports every credential name before launch, empty unless the
# project's HARNESS uses it, which overrides anything set in this file. What
# follows only serves raw `bin/harness` callers such as scripts.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Headless Claude Code auth, generated on the host with `claude setup-token`.
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
